.\" vertrice(7): voidrice on OpenBSD for the ThinkPad X220.
.\" Licensed under the GNU GPL, version 3, as the rest of vertrice.
.Dd $Mdocdate: September 29 2026 $
.Dt VERTRICE 7
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm vertrice
.Nd voidrice dotfiles for OpenBSD on the ThinkPad X220
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is voidrice, a set of dotfiles for Linux, ported to
.Ox
and set up for a ThinkPad X220.
It keeps the voidrice layout: scripts in
.Pa ~/.local/bin ,
configuration in
.Pa ~/.config ,
dmenu for every menu and one status line.
It uses the base system first:
.Xr ksh 1
is the shell,
.Xr cwm 1
the window manager and
.Xr xterm 1
the terminal.
A package is added only for a feature base does not have.
.Ss Install
The dotfiles are a bare git repository whose work tree is the home
directory.
On a fresh system, as root:
.Pp
.Dl # pkg_add git
.Pp
Then, as the user:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ git clone --bare https://github.com/stokesgeo/vertrice.git \e
    ~/.local/share/vertrice.git
$ git --git-dir=$HOME/.local/share/vertrice.git \e
    --work-tree=$HOME checkout -f
$ git --git-dir=$HOME/.local/share/vertrice.git \e
    config status.showUntrackedFiles no
.Ed
.Pp
The checkout replaces the
.Pa .profile
that
.Xr adduser 8
copied in.
The system half is
.Pa ~/.local/bin/vertrice-install ,
a plain list of commands.
Read it, then run it as root:
.Pp
.Dl $ doas sh ~/.local/bin/vertrice-install
.Pp
The first time there is no
.Xr doas.conf 5
yet: use
.Ic su -
and run the file by its full path.
It uses the files in
.Pa ~/.local/share/openbsd
and does the following:
.Bl -dash
.It
installs the packages in
.Pa pkglist
with
.Xr pkg_add 1 ;
.It
writes
.Pa /etc/doas.conf
from
.Pa doas.conf
and
.Pa doas-agent.conf ,
after
.Ic doas -C
accepts them;
.It
installs
.Pa /root/.kshrc
(vi editing and a red prompt for
.Ic doas -s ) ;
.It
installs
.Pa /etc/login.conf.d/staff ,
which raises the memory and open-file limits of the staff class for
the browsers;
.It
installs
.Pa /etc/pf.conf
after
.Ic pfctl -nf
accepts it, and loads it;
.It
installs
.Pa /etc/apm/suspend ,
with
.Pa /etc/apm/hibernate
as a link to it, and
.Pa /etc/hotplug/attach ;
.It
adds a line to root's crontab that counts waiting updates, and a
.Xr calendar 1
line to the user's crontab;
.It
adds
.Dq root: Ar user
to
.Pa /etc/mail/aliases ,
unless root already has an alias, and runs
.Xr newaliases 8 ;
.It
enables
.Xr apmd 8
(with
.Fl z Ar 7 ) ,
.Xr hotplugd 8 ,
messagebus,
.Xr obsdfreqd 1
and
.Xr unwind 8 ;
.It
appends its lines to
.Pa /etc/wsconsctl.conf
and
.Pa /etc/fbtab .
.El
.Pp
Reboot afterwards.
Running it again is safe: the appended lines repeat, and the last one
read wins.
.Pp
The optional packages (mail, news, passwords, torrents, downloads, the
dictionary and others) are in a second list:
.Pp
.Dl $ doas pkg_add -l ~/.local/share/openbsd/pkglist.extra
.Pp
After them,
.Ic doas sh ~/.local/bin/vertrice-dict
builds the dictionary once.
.Pp
The shell function
.Ic config
is
.Xr git 1
with that repository and the home directory as its work tree.
Update with:
.Pp
.Dl $ config pull origin master
.Pp
The bare clone has no fetch refspec, so the remote and branch are named.
Add files by name, never with
.Ic config add .\&
in the home directory.
After an update that changes
.Pa ~/.local/share/openbsd ,
run the installer again.
.Ss Session
Logging in on
.Pa /dev/ttyC0
runs
.Xr startx 1 ;
.Xr xenodm 1
works too, through
.Pa ~/.xsession .
The session starts a D-Bus session bus, runs
.Pa ~/.config/x11/xprofile ,
then
.Xr cwm 1 .
.Ev WM Ns = Ns Cm dwm
in the profile runs dwm instead, with
.Ic sbar
writing the status line; dwm and st are built by hand into
.Pa ~/.local/src .
.Pp
The xprofile sets the wallpaper and palette, starts mpd and dunst,
runs
.Ic remaps ,
starts
.Xr xidle 1 ,
which locks the screen after ten idle minutes or when the pointer
rests in the top-left corner, and shows a notice when a USB disk is
attached or a backup is due.
.Ss Keys
The key list is
.Pa ~/.config/cwm/cwmrc ;
.Ic 4-F1
shows it in dmenu.
In its notation 4 is Super, S is Shift and C is Control.
voidrice's dwm keys are kept: groups are dwm's tags, and windows float
until
.Ic 4-t
tiles them.
cwm has no bar, so
.Ic 4-b
shows the status line as a notification.
The keys that differ from voidrice:
.Bl -tag -width "4C-F11" -offset indent
.It Ic 4-Return
.Ic sd :
a terminal in the folder of the focused window's program, or in home.
The helper that finds the folder,
.Pa ~/.local/src/sd/proc-cwd ,
is built on first use.
.It Ic 4S-F1
.Ic manpick :
pick any manual page in dmenu.
.It Ic 4S-F2
.Ic writemode :
full-screen nvim in Goyo on the last file changed in
.Pa ~/writing .
.It Ic 4-F4
.Ic nightlight :
a warm screen, on or off.
.It Ic 4-F8
.Ic theme toggle :
the day or night palette.
.It Ic 4-F11
.Xr video 1 :
the webcam view.
.It Ic 4C-F11
.Ic rectoggle :
turn the microphone and camera on for a call, or off again.
It asks for the doas password in a terminal.
It is not named rec because sox has a rec command.
.It Ic 4S-F11
.Ic dmenuwifi :
join a wireless network picked in dmenu, and offer to add it to
.Pa /etc/hostname.\& Ns Ar if
when that file exists.
.It Ic 4-F12
.Ic remaps :
the keyboard and TrackPoint settings again.
.El
.Ss Machine settings
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Touchpad
Off:
.Cm mouse.tp.disable=1
in
.Pa /etc/wsconsctl.conf .
The TrackPoint is the pointer; hold its middle button and push to
scroll.
.It Caps Lock
Types Escape on the console
.Pq Xr wsconsctl.conf 5 .
In X,
.Ic remaps
makes it Escape when tapped and Super when held, as in voidrice.
.It Recording
Off, as
.Ox
ships it
.Pq Va kern.audio.record , kern.video.record .
.Ic rectoggle
turns both on and off.
.Pa /etc/fbtab
gives the camera to whoever logs in on the console.
.It Suspend
.Xr apmd 8
runs
.Pa /etc/apm/suspend
before sleeping, and it locks X first.
.Ic zzz
suspends,
.Ic ZZZ
hibernates, and apmd suspends at 7% battery.
.It CPU speed
.Xr obsdfreqd 1 ,
at full speed on power and half on battery.
.It Firewall
.Xr pf.conf 5
blocks all that comes in unasked and passes all that goes out.
.Ic pfctl -sr
shows the rules.
.El
.Ss Mail
Root's mail, from
.Xr daily 8
and root's
.Xr cron 8
jobs, goes to the user, in
.Pa /var/mail/ Ns Ar user ,
with the user's own cron mail.
Read it with
.Xr mail 1 .
For neomutt, add
.Ql mailboxes /var/mail/ Ns Ar user
to your own muttrc.
.Ss Reminders
Reminders go in
.Pa ~/.calendar/calendar ,
one to a line: a date, a tab, the text.
Comments are written
.Ql /* ... */ .
The nightly run of
.Xr daily 8
at 01:30 calls
.Ql calendar -a
and mails you the lines for today and tomorrow; on Friday, through
Monday.
Codex in
.Ic cdxb
may add reminders there.
.Ss Dictionary
.Ic dict Ar word
shows the definitions from GCIDE and the Roget's Thesaurus (1911)
headings that hold the word.
.Ic dict -d gcide Ar word
shows the definitions only;
.Ic roget Ar word
shows the Roget headings only.
In nvim,
.Ic K
on a word in Markdown or text looks it up.
.Xr dictd 8
listens on localhost only.
.Ss Backups
.Ic bk full
and
.Ic bk incr
write a level 0 or level 1
.Xr dump 8
of
.Pa /home ,
compressed, to
.Pa /mnt/backup/dump .
Mount the backup disk on
.Pa /mnt/backup
first
.Pq Ic 4-F9 .
On a new FFS disk, make the folder yours once:
.Ic doas install -d -o $USER -m 700 /mnt/backup/dump .
.Ic dump -W
shows the last dumps.
At login,
.Ic dump -w
decides whether to show the reminder.
It follows the dump-frequency field of the
.Pa /home
line in
.Xr fstab 5 :
the
.Ox
installer writes 1, a daily reminder; set it to 7 for a weekly one.
Read a dump back with
.Ic gzip -dc Ar file | Ic restore -tf - .
.Ss Writing
.Bl -tag -width "writemode" -compact
.It Ic spellcheck Ar file
.Xr spell 1 ,
each flagged word shown in its line.
Your own words go in
.Pa ~/.local/share/spell/words ,
sorted with
.Ic sort -f .
.It Ic dupwords Ar file
Doubled words, across line ends.
.It Ic proof Op Ar file
spellcheck, dupwords,
.Xr diction 1
and
.Xr style 1
in one pager.
.It Ic writemode
Full-screen writing
.Pq Ic 4S-F2 .
.It Ic sb-words
The word count of the last file changed in
.Pa ~/writing .
.El
.Ss Downloads and archives
.Ic qndl
queues downloads with
.Xr nq 1 ,
one after another;
.Ic sb-tasks
counts them.
.Ic ext Ar file ...
extracts archives with
.Xr bsdtar 1
and keeps existing files.
.Ss Themes
.Ic theme day
and
.Ic theme night
set the palette of the terminals, dunst and zathura.
At login the palette follows the clock: day from 07:00, night from 19:00.
.Ev PALETTE Ns = Ns Cm wal
in the profile takes the colours from the wallpaper with pywal instead.
.Ss Updates
Every four hours root's crontab writes what
.Xr syspatch 8
and
.Ic pkg_add -u
would install to
.Pa /var/db/updates .
.Ic sb-updates
counts it in the status line;
.Ic sb-popupgrade
installs the updates in a terminal.
.Ss Codex in a box
.Ic cdxb
runs Codex from your own terminal in a box made with
.Xr unveil 2
and
.Xr pledge 2 .
Codex and all it runs see the system read-only,
.Pa ~/.codex ,
the working directory, the paths in
.Pa ~/.config/cdxb/grants
and those given with options.
The paths in
.Pa ~/.config/cdxb/deny
stay hidden, and the box's own settings and your dotfiles stay
read-only.
Codex proposes a change to a settings file by writing it whole;
.Ic cdxb review
shows the diff and applies it on y.
Git runs the hooks and commands a repository's
.Pa .git
names, and Codex may change any
.Pa .git
it can write: in those repositories git is Codex's job, done in the box.
.Pp
.Ic cdxb
.Op Fl adH
.Op Fl r Ar path
.Op Fl w Ar path
.Op Ar dir Op Ar codex-arg ...
.Bl -tag -width "-w path" -offset indent
.It Fl a
Codex asks before any command it does not know to be safe.
.It Fl d
Codex may run the nopass rules of
.Pa doas-agent.conf ,
as
.Ic cdxb doas Ar command ,
through a relay outside the box.
.It Fl H
Allow
.Ar dir
to be the home directory.
All of home but the deny list becomes readable, and each folder in it
writable but
.Pa ~/.cache ,
.Pa ~/.config
and
.Pa ~/.local .
.It Fl r Ar path
Codex may read
.Ar path .
.It Fl w Ar path
Codex may change
.Ar path .
.El
.Pp
.Ic cdxb add
.Op Fl r
.Ar path Op Ar session
gives a running session one more path: quit that Codex and it resumes
with the path.
.Ic cdxb ls
lists the running sessions.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It Pa ~/.local/share/vertrice.git
The bare repository.
.It Pa ~/.local/bin/vertrice-install
The system half of the install.
.It Pa ~/.local/share/openbsd/
The files it installs, and the package lists
.Pa pkglist
and
.Pa pkglist.extra .
.It Pa ~/.config/cwm/cwmrc
The keys.
.It Pa ~/.config/shell/profile
.Ev WM ,
.Ev TERMINAL
and
.Ev MANPATH .
.It Pa ~/.calendar/calendar
Reminders.
.It Pa ~/.config/cdxb/grants , ~/.config/cdxb/deny
What the Codex box may use, and what it hides.
.It Pa ~/.local/share/man/man7/vertrice.7
This page.
The profile's
.Ev MANPATH
starts with a colon, so
.Xr man 1
searches the standard path first, then
.Pa ~/.local/share/man .
.It Pa ~/.local/share/vertrice/reading
Small base programs worth reading: the manual first, then the source.
.It Pa ~/.local/share/vertrice/tests/
The regression suite
.Pq Pa run ,
the check on the machine
.Pq Pa check
and the porting notes
.Pq Pa OPENBSD.md .
.It Pa /var/db/updates
Waiting updates, one to a line.
.It Pa /etc/dumpdates
The dumps done so far.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
A reminder for the third of October, in
.Pa ~/.calendar/calendar ,
with a tab after the date:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
Oct 3	Return the library books
.Ed
.Pp
Look a word up in the thesaurus:
.Pp
.Dl $ roget pity
.Pp
Proofread the last file changed in
.Pa ~/writing :
.Pp
.Dl $ proof
.Pp
Run Codex in a project with read access to a reference tree:
.Pp
.Dl $ cdxb -r ~/src/lib ~/src/project
.Pp
Make
.Xr apropos 1
and
.Ic manpick
find this page:
.Pp
.Dl $ makewhatis ~/.local/share/man
